 "_changes_20aug": [
  "HINGE anchor is now the Romanian Deadlift, and a separate GLUTE ladder anchors on the Hip Thrust \u2014 hip thrust produces roughly 229% MVC glute activation against the back squat's 130%, with no bar on the spine.",
  "SQUAT gains the Spanish Squat: loads the quad hard with minimal patellofemoral compression, and is analgesic on the patellar tendon.",
  "PUSH-UP gains straight-bar push-up (easier) and dead-stop (harder), both yours.",
  "PLANCHE removed \u2014 your call: fundamentals are the forever exercises, not calisthenics skills.",
  "FRONT LEVER anchor is now the band-assisted version, reps not a hold, as you asked.",
  "ROTATION reworked. Pallof press is ANTI-rotation (isometric resist) and has been moved to its own ladder; true rotation is the woodchop, chop and med-ball throw.",
  "CARRY: suitcase carry moved from regression to progression \u2014 it is the harder one to stabilise.",
  "BURPEE gains the 5- and 7-pump Navy Seals.",
  "JUMP SQUAT gains the lateral bound (the skater jump you meant) and the jumping reverse lunge."
 ]
